+# Connecting account passkeys
+
+The provided site is static. It opens a clearly labeled demo account, persists demo passkeys in localStorage, and never signals demo credentials to a real authenticator. No authentication server is included.
+
+To enable live mode, set the `api-base` meta element in index.html to a same-origin authenticated account API, such as `/api/account`. Optionally inject a `csrf-token` meta element from your server. Replace the demo account sections and enforce authentication on the account route before production use.
+
+Implement these endpoints:
+
+- `GET /passkeys`: return the signed-in customer's complete passkey snapshot.
+- `PATCH /passkeys/:id`: accept `{ "name": "Work laptop" }` and return the updated complete snapshot.
+- `DELETE /passkeys/:id`: delete the server credential and return the complete snapshot after deletion.
+- `POST /passkeys/registration/options`: accept `{ "name": "Work laptop" }`; return WebAuthn creation options in JSON format, with base64url binary fields.
+- `POST /passkeys/registration/verify`: accept `{ "name": "Work laptop", "credential": <WebAuthn credential JSON> }`; verify the challenge and credential, save it, and return the complete snapshot.
+
+Snapshot format:
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "coffee.example.com",
+  "user": {
+    "id": "BASE64URL_WEBAUTHN_USER_HANDLE",
+    "name": "Jamie Davis",
+    "email": "jamie@example.com",
+    "initials": "JD"
+  },
+  "passkeys": [{
+    "id": "BASE64URL_CREDENTIAL_ID",
+    "name": "Work laptop",
+    "device": "laptop",
+    "provider": "iCloud Keychain",
+    "created": "2026-10-12T10:00:00Z",
+    "lastUsed": "2026-11-02T12:00:00Z",
+    "current": true
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+Use the actual WebAuthn user handle, credential IDs, and relying party ID. Enforce session ownership, CSRF protections, validation, appropriate reauthentication, and any last-sign-in-method policy on the server. Return 401 for expired sessions and errors for rejected mutations. Mutation responses must contain the full authoritative credential list; do not paginate it. Never return secrets or private keys.
+
+After an authenticated list or successful mutation, the UI calls `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials` when available. It never sends an optimistic or demo list. A failed or unsupported sync does not undo server deletion; the UI explains manual password manager cleanup and provides retry on failure. Per-device nicknames do not rename user account identity in authenticators, so renaming does not call `signalCurrentUserDetails`.
+
+Run `npm run build` to check JavaScript syntax and copy static assets to `dist/`, including an `/account/` entry. No server is started.
